# Example 03: a cryo-EM map, two ways.
# PDB 7S4X with EMD-24838, a Cas9 checkpoint state from the Taylor lab.
#
# Panel A, overview: opaque map surface colored by the domain colors of the
# model inside it, via color zone. No model shown, no mesh, no silhouettes.
# Panel B, zoom: the model opaque with its own density drawn semi-transparent
# in the same color on top, which is how you show that density supports a
# feature without hiding the feature.
open 7s4x
open emdb:24838
open ../../palettes/lab_colors.cxc
open ../../presets/Base/publication_white.cxc

# Color the model first: color zone copies these colors onto the map surface
select /A
open ../../palettes/cas9_domains.cxc
select clear
color /B lab_sgrna
color /C,c lab_target
color /D lab_nontarget

view #1
turn y 30
view pad 0.05

# --- Panel A: segmented opaque map ---
hide #1 models
volume #2 style surface level 0.08 step 1
color zone #2 near #1 distance 6 sharpEdges true
graphics silhouettes false
lighting soft
key lab_rec1:REC1 lab_rec2:REC2 lab_rec3:REC3 lab_hnh:HNH lab_ruvc:RuvC lab_pi:PI lab_sgrna:sgRNA "lab_target:target DNA" "lab_nontarget:non-target" pos 0.03,0.08 size 0.025,0.45 fontSize 16 colorTreatment distinct labelSide right/bottom labelOffset 4
2dlabels text "EMD-24838  2.8 Å" xpos 0.04 ypos 0.94 size 20 color lab_black bold true
save map_overview.png width 1800 supersample 3

# --- Panel B: model with its own density on top ---
key delete
2dlabels delete all
show #1 models
graphics silhouettes true width 1.5
color zone #2 near #1 distance 6 sharpEdges true
volume #2 transparency 0.65
# zone the map to the HNH domain so the panel shows one thing
volume zone #2 nearAtoms /A:775-908 range 3
view /A:775-908
view pad 0.12
2dlabels text "HNH  density" xpos 0.04 ypos 0.94 size 20 color lab_black bold true
save map_zoom.png width 1800 supersample 3
